      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="portfolio-grid case-study-layout">
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Project Overview</span>
              <h2>What the system does and why teams depended on it</h2>
              <p>Teamery is a saas platform built for teams that need a focused workspace for project coordination and internal visibility. The product was designed to replace fragmented task tracking and scattered communication with a more structured team workspace.</p>
              <p>From an engineering perspective, the system had to support daily team usage, repeated task updates, and workspace visibility without burdening users with tool complexity. That made it a production platform with real operational demands rather than a portfolio demo.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Business Challenge</span>
              <h2>What had to improve for the product to scale cleanly</h2>
              <p>The core business challenge was delivering a product that could serve collaboration software and productivity systems use cases while still remaining easy for operators to trust and use every day.</p>
              <p>The client wanted a product that was simple enough for teams to adopt quickly while still providing meaningful operational clarity.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
